            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of postcraniectomy orthostatic headache with lumbar epidural blood patches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>730-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postcraniectomy orthostatic headache is a rare, but disabling, condition which can often interfere with patient rehabilitation. Previously, postsurgical CSF leaks have generally been managed with surgical repair. We present the case of a 32-year-old man with postcraniectomy orthostatic headache which was successively managed with repeated lumbar epidural blood patches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
